	'ip_ct_st_p' => 'Aiko Brennan, stallholder coordinator, answers questions on stalls, gate passes, access and ticket transfers.',
	'ip_faq_a1' => 'Early-bird pricing for the 2027 Hozue Food Festival ends on Friday 30 April 2027 at 24:00 midnight. After this deadline, standard admission rates apply for both single day and full weekend tickets. Early-bird day passes cost €24 compared to the regular €32, while weekend tickets cost €40 instead of €54. All ticket transactions are completed securely online through our website, with digital passes delivered directly by email within ten minutes of purchase.',
	'ip_faq_a10' => 'Children under 12 years of age receive free admission to Hozue Food Festival when accompanied by an adult ticket holder. We also offer a Family Weekend pass covering two adults and up to three children for both days at €88 early-bird or €112 regular pricing. Children under 12 do not require a paid ticket, but must be accompanied by a responsible adult while exploring the market stalls and riverbank lawns.',
	'ip_faq_a11' => 'Sunday afternoon features a dedicated family picnic gathering on the central lawn starting at 12:30. Families can spread out picnic rugs, enjoy fresh fruit and sweet pastries from our bakery stalls, and participate in open lawn games. Step-free access makes navigating prams and pushchairs around the grass lawns straightforward. Clean, accessible family restrooms and handwashing stations are located nearby, adjacent to the willow grove and the Weir Lane entrance.',
	'ip_faq_a12' => 'Well-behaved dogs on short, fixed leads are welcome within the open outdoor areas of Hozue Riverside Park throughout the weekend. We ask dog owners to keep their animals under close control on the lawns and away from crowded food preparation counters. Due to food hygiene standards, pets are not permitted inside enclosed food marquees or within the Wine Tent, with the exception of certified assistance dogs assisting visitors.',
	'ip_faq_a2' => 'Tickets can be transferred to another person until 1 September 2027 at no extra charge. If you need to reassign your pass, email stallholder coordinator Aiko Brennan at hello@hozuefestival.example with your booking confirmation number and the replacement guest details. Under our standard terms, full cancellations and refunds are permitted up until 1 August 2027. After 1 August, tickets cannot be refunded, though they remain eligible for transfer until the 1 September cutoff date.',
	'ip_faq_a3' => 'The tasting pass is an optional add-on available for €18 during the early-bird period and €22 at regular pricing. It entitles the holder to eight individual wine tastings across our eighteen participating winemakers, as well as an official festival tasting glass to keep. You can collect your glassware and tasting tokens at the Wine Tent desk inside Hozue Riverside Park by presenting your festival entry wristband upon arrival.',
	'ip_faq_a4' => 'The festival runs on Saturday 11 September 2027 from 11:00 to 21:00, and on Sunday 12 September 2027 from 11:00 to 18:00. Advance ticket holders benefit from early gate opening thirty minutes before general admission, beginning at 10:30 on both Saturday and Sunday mornings. We recommend arriving during this early window to collect your wristband smoothly at the Weir Lane entrance and explore the morning market stalls before peak afternoon hours.',
	'ip_faq_a5' => 'The festival is located at Hozue Riverside Park on Weir Lane in Alderford. Visitors travelling by train can take regional services to Alderford station, which is an easy eight-minute walk along signposted footpaths to the main Weir Lane gate. Cyclists can cross the river footbridge directly to our temporary bicycle parking racks. Limited car parking is available in the north meadow on Weir Lane, though public rail travel or car sharing is strongly encouraged.',
	'ip_faq_a6' => 'Your general admission ticket covers entry to Hozue Riverside Park, access to the programme talks, and lawn entertainment. All food portions, meals, and drinks purchased at the sixty-four independent producer stalls are paid for directly on the day. Stallholders accept debit cards and cash at their individual counters. For wine tasting in the Wine Tent, guests can either use their prepaid tasting pass tokens or purchase pours directly from the eighteen independent winemakers.',
	'ip_faq_a7' => 'Our sixty-four food and drink stalls are run by independent regional producers who prepare their own recipes from scratch. Because our producers harvest and cook their own goods, they have detailed knowledge of all ingredients and potential allergens. You will find clear gluten-free, dairy-free, vegetarian, and vegan options across the market garden, bakery, and grill sections. We advise visitors with severe allergies to speak directly with cooks at individual counters before placing orders.',
	'ip_faq_a8' => 'The Saturday long-table lunch takes place at 13:00 along the communal riverside table in Hozue Riverside Park. The ticket costs €45 during early-bird sales and €52 at regular pricing. It includes three seasonal courses highlighting seasonal ingredients provided by our market gardeners, bakers, and regional cooks. Because seating at the riverside table is strictly limited, we advise reserving your lunch ticket when purchasing your festival admission pass online to secure your seat at the table.',
	'ip_faq_a9' => 'While we welcome blankets and small picnic accessories on the festival lawns, we encourage visitors to support our sixty-four local producers, bakers, and cooks who bring their harvests to the park. Small snacks for young children and reusable water bottles are fully permitted. Free freshwater refill stations are stationed beside the Weir Lane gate and near the Wine Tent. Outside alcoholic beverages are strictly prohibited across the festival grounds under local park regulations.',
