	'ip_programme_h1' => 'Festival Programme',
	'ip_programme_lede' => 'The 2027 festival runs across two calm, flavour-filled days at Hozue Riverside Park on Saturday 11 and Sunday 12 September. Gates open thirty minutes earlier for advance ticket holders, with events unfolding along the water from morning until dusk.',
	'ip_programme_s1_b' => 'Saturday gates open at 10:30 for ticket holders, with general entry running from 11:00 until 21:00. The morning market begins promptly at 11:00, showcasing regional growers and fresh produce stalls. At 13:00, guests gather for the long-table lunch, featuring three seasonal courses served along the riverbank table. From 16:00, the Wine Tent tastings open under the canvas, where eighteen winemakers pour selections from their cellars, including Tomás Achterberg pouring Achterberg Hill vintages. Throughout the afternoon, acoustic music on the lawn provides a gentle background, allowing guests to relax on the grass while enjoying seasonal dishes.',
	'ip_programme_s1_h' => 'Saturday 11 September Programme',
	'ip_programme_s2_b' => 'Sunday welcomes visitors from 11:00 to 18:00, with advance ticket holder entry beginning at 10:30. At 11:00, the day opens with bread and fire, as Sven Lindahl bakes fresh wood-fired sourdough beside the open hearths. At 12:30, families gather across the family picnic lawn for relaxed dining, fruit stalls, and open-air lawn games. Informal cooking talks run beside the market stalls from early afternoon, offering practical techniques from local cooks like Priya Ramanathan. The weekend concludes at 17:00 with the river terrace last pour, offering one final shared glass as the afternoon sun settles over the water.',
	'ip_programme_s2_h' => 'Sunday 12 September Programme',
	'ip_programme_s3_b' => 'Beyond the scheduled tastings and meals, informal gatherings take place across the park both days. Acoustic musicians play unamplified sets on the open lawn, creating an easy, conversational setting where friends can linger over shared platters. Near the market garden stalls, cooks host practical cooking talks, discussing seasonal produce, fire management, and simple fermentation methods. There is no need to book separate passes for the lawn music or talks; they are open to all day and weekend ticket holders. Guests are welcome to drop by, ask questions, taste samples, and enjoy the relaxed riverside pace.',
