	'ip_st_colh2' => 'Dairy, garden and sweets',
	'ip_stallholders_caps' => 'Stallholders',
	'ip_stallholders_h1' => 'Our Stallholders',
	'ip_stallholders_lede' => 'Our sixty-four independent stalls and eighteen winemakers represent the finest agricultural and culinary producers from across the region. Each stallholder brings their own harvest, cellar, or kitchen craft to the riverbank for this tenth edition.',
	'ip_stallholders_s1_b' => 'The festival grounds are organised into six dedicated producer categories, bringing together sixty-four distinct stalls across the park. The wine sector features eighteen independent winemakers pouring regional vintages. The grill section includes twelve stalls preparing seasonal meats and fire-cooked skewers. Eight bakeries showcase wood-fired sourdough, traditional loaves, and heritage grains. Six dairy producers feature farmhouse cheeses and fresh yoghurts. Twelve market garden stalls bring ripe tomatoes, runner beans, and fresh field greens picked at dawn. Finally, eight sweet stalls present fruit tarts, local honeys, and artisan preserves. Every vendor sells their own produce directly.',
	'ip_stallholders_s1_h' => 'Sixty-Four Stalls by Category',
	'ip_stallholders_s2_b' => 'Among our sixty-four stallholders are makers who have shaped the festival since its early days. Market gardener Joseph Mwangi brings morning crates of heirloom tomatoes and fresh runner beans directly from his fields. Baker Sven Lindahl tends the wood-fired oven on the grass, baking crusty loaves of country sourdough for Sunday visitors. Cook Priya Ramanathan prepares fire-grilled skewers over seasoned wood, pairing fresh seasonal ingredients with gentle aromatic spices. Cheesemaker Hélène Varga cuts wheels of washed-rind cheeses at her counter, sharing traditional curing methods from her small regional dairy with curious visitors.',
	'ip_stallholders_s2_h' => 'Growers, Bakers, and Cooks',
	'ip_stallholders_s3_b' => 'Festival founder and director Marguerite Ostby works alongside our stallholder coordinator Aiko Brennan to curate the sixty-four stalls and assist producers throughout the weekend. Aiko manages producer logistics, transfer requests, and vendor accessibility requirements. At the Wine Tent, eighteen independent vintners pour their vintages, led by winemaker Tomás Achterberg from Achterberg Hill, who shares his light white wines across the timber counter. Our producers share a commitment to honest farming, patient fermentation, and direct conversation with everyone who visits their stalls along the Weir Lane riverbank.',
	'ip_stallholders_s3_h' => 'Winemakers and Coordination',
	'ip_stallholders_tile1' => 'Categories',
	'ip_stallholders_tile2' => 'Makers',
	'ip_stallholders_tile3' => 'Winemakers',
	'ip_stallholders_tile4' => 'Tickets',
	'ip_terms_h1' => 'Terms and Conditions',
	'ip_terms_lede' => 'These terms and conditions govern ticket purchases, entry requirements, and visitor conduct for Hozue Food Festival in Alderford. By purchasing a ticket or entering Hozue Riverside Park, you agree to comply with the regulations outlined below.',
	'ip_terms_s1_b' => 'All tickets for Hozue Food Festival are sold subject to our standard cancellation and transfer rules. Full refunds are available upon written request until 1 August 2027. After 1 August 2027, ticket purchases are non-refundable. However, tickets may be transferred to another individual at no additional cost until 1 September 2027. To transfer a ticket, the original purchaser must notify stallholder coordinator Aiko Brennan at hello@hozuefestival.example with the order number and the replacement guest name. Tickets presented at the Weir Lane gate will be exchanged for non-transferable entry wristbands.',
	'ip_terms_s1_h' => 'Ticket Refunds and Transfer Policy',
	'ip_terms_s2_b' => 'Hozue Food Festival takes place outdoors in Hozue Riverside Park on Saturday 11 and Sunday 12 September 2027. The festival proceeds rain or shine. In the event of inclement weather, covered marquees, sheltered dining tables, and marquee pavilions ensure tastings and activities continue safely. Ticket holders must wear their official fabric wristband at all times within the grounds. The festival management reserves the right to refuse entry or remove any individual whose behaviour endangers others, damages park grounds, or infringes on our quiet riverside community atmosphere.',
	'ip_terms_s2_h' => 'Weather Policy and Park Regulations',
	'ip_thanks_btn' => 'Back to the festival home',
	'ip_thanks_h1' => 'Thank You for Your Order',
	'ip_thanks_lede' => 'Your order for Hozue Food Festival has been successfully processed and confirmed. We look forward to welcoming you to Hozue Riverside Park in Alderford on Saturday 11 and Sunday 12 September 2027.',
	'ip_thanks_s1_b' => 'Thank you for purchasing your tickets for Hozue Food Festival. Your official e-ticket will arrive in your email inbox within ten minutes of purchase. Please check your junk or spam folder if the confirmation email does not appear promptly in your main inbox. The email contains your booking reference number and a scannable digital barcode. You do not need to print your e-ticket; simply present the barcode on your mobile smartphone screen at the Weir Lane entrance gate upon your arrival at Hozue Riverside Park.',
	'ip_thanks_s1_h' => 'Your E-Ticket Arrives Within 10 Minutes',
	'ip_thanks_s2_b' => 'Festival gates open on Saturday 11 September from 11:00 to 21:00, and on Sunday 12 September from 11:00 to 18:00. Advance ticket holders are invited to enter thirty minutes early, beginning at 10:30 each morning. If you purchased a tasting pass add-on, your wristband will allow you to collect your eight tasting tokens and keepsake wine glass inside the Wine Tent. To review travel directions, train connections, or the full weekend schedule, you can return to our programme page or browse our visitor guide.',
	'ip_thanks_s2_h' => 'Preparing for Your Riverside Visit',
	'ip_tickets_caps' => 'Tickets',
	'ip_tickets_h1' => 'Festival Tickets',
	'ip_tickets_lede' => 'Advance early-bird tickets for the 2027 Hozue Food Festival are available online until Friday 30 April 2027 at midnight. Choose your preferred pass below to join us along the riverbank in Alderford on 11 and 12 September.',
	'ip_tickets_s1_b' => 'We offer clear admission options for individuals, wine enthusiasts, and families. Early-bird prices apply through Friday 30 April 2027 at midnight; thereafter, regular rates apply.',
	'ip_tickets_s1_h' => 'Ticket Options and Pricing',
	'ip_tickets_s2_b' => 'Attending the festival is simple and entirely digital. First, choose your ticket type, selecting a day ticket, full weekend ticket, or family pass. Second, pay securely online, and your official e-ticket will arrive in your email inbox within ten minutes of purchase. Third, when you arrive at Hozue Riverside Park, show the digital barcode on your mobile screen or paper printout at the Weir Lane gate to receive your fabric entry wristband. Fourth, if you purchased a tasting pass add-on, present your wristband inside the Wine Tent to collect your eight tasting tokens and your tasting glass to keep.',
	'ip_tickets_s2_h' => 'How Your Ticket Works',
	'ip_tickets_s3_b' => 'All festival admission passes can be transferred to another guest until 1 September 2027 without penalty or processing fees. If you can no longer attend, simply send an email to stallholder coordinator Aiko Brennan at hello@hozuefestival.example with your order details and the new guest name. For group bookings of ten or more visitors, or for guests requiring tailored accessibility arrangements, please submit your request with the booking form below. Our festival team will confirm availability and assist you with step-free entrance passes and reserved seating where needed.',
	'ip_tickets_s3_h' => 'Transfer Rules and Group Enquiries',
