	'wk_caps' => 'The weekend',
	'wk_h2' => 'Two days of seasonal food, wine, and craft along the water',
	'wk_p1' => 'Every September, growers, cooks, and winemakers assemble along Weir Lane to share the harvest across two unhurried days in Hozue Riverside Park. The festival grounds stretch between the willow-lined riverbank and open lawns, creating a welcoming outdoor kitchen where seasonal dishes are cooked over open coals and served straight from the fire.',
	'wk_p2' => 'Eighteen regional vintners pour low-intervention wines alongside market stalls laden with heirloom vegetables, ripe cheeses, and wood-fired breads. Visitors gather along the communal river table to taste new vintages, exchange recipes, and meet the independent producers whose daily craft sustains the surrounding agricultural valleys and meadows.',
	'wk_p3' => 'Now celebrating its 10th edition since Marguerite Ostby founded the gathering in 2016, the weekend retains its original neighbourhood scale and gentle rhythm. With sixty-four independent stalls, one keepsake tasting glass, and shared riverbank meals, the gathering offers an authentic taste of place grounded in community stewardship.',
